WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:06.480
In most events, like conferences and concerts,
a person with a mic may come close to a speaker.

2
00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:08.720
The mic picks up the speaker.

3
00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:12.180
The sound loops back, builds, and then it howls.

4
00:00:12.525 --> 00:00:17.005
Today, engineers pull the fader down,
or they notch out frequencies.

5
00:00:17.275 --> 00:00:18.895
That costs you volume.

6
00:00:19.055 --> 00:00:20.535
And it costs you tone.

7
00:00:20.883 --> 00:00:25.083
Nullyn AI sits inline, between the mic and the console.

8
00:00:25.373 --> 00:00:28.423
It listens to the mic, and to the speaker feed.

9
00:00:28.783 --> 00:00:34.123
It predicts the feedback path in real time,
and it takes the loop out before it rings.

10
00:00:34.383 --> 00:00:37.123
So the voice and the instruments stay natural.

11
00:00:37.476 --> 00:00:42.076
Version one runs on a laptop, with a USB audio interface.

12
00:00:42.376 --> 00:00:45.286
Version two is our own dedicated box.

13
00:00:45.476 --> 00:00:47.766
Version three deploys at scale.

14
00:00:48.158 --> 00:00:52.638
Nullyn AI. More gain before feedback,
without wrecking the sound.

15
00:00:52.976 --> 00:00:54.216
nullyn.ai
